subgraph four["Logging Workout Process"]
        E1["Logging Workout Process"]
        E2["Individual daily workouts appear as cards below the 'Current Week: Week X' section and each card contains details (exercises, sets, reps/rep ranges, tempo, etc.)"]
        E2A@{ label: "Quick actions: 'Quick Log' button appears for simple/repeated workouts"}
        E2B@{ label: "Quick log flow: Single-tap logging for exercises with previous weights/reps"}
        E3["Each daily workout card **IN THE CURRENT WEEK ONLY** has a 'Log Workout' button"]
        E4["For example, if user has not completed all Week 1 workouts and selects to view the Week 2 workouts, only the Week 1 workouts will have the 'Log Workout' button"]
        E5["User clicks 'Log Workout' button for one of the workouts"]
        E6["That daily workout's details are then displayed and fill the page"]
        E7["As user completes a workout, they input weight and reps for each set of each exercise/lift"]
        E8["At bottom of the workout logs, user then measures energy level, difficulty, and satisfaction levels for that day"]
        E9["Once the full workout is logged, user clicks 'Save Workout Log' button at bottom"]
        E10["Daily workout data is saved and stored to database"]
        E10A@{ label: "Micro-celebration: Workout completion animation + progress ring update"}
        E11["Automatically redirects back to the main /workouts/plans page"]
        E12["The now completed and logged workout no longer appears under the 'Current Week: Week X' section, but instead appears under the 'Logged Workouts' section w/ a completion checkmark and a 'View Logged Workout' button"]  
        E13["Message appears temporarily at bottom of screen saying (Successfully completed and logged workout. You can view this workout log under 'Logged Workouts')"]      
  end
subgraph five["All Workouts for Week Completed Logic"]
        F1["Completing Final Workout of Week Logic - using Week 1 as example"]
        F2["'Current Week: Week 1' section contains one final card and all other daily workouts in Week 1 appear under 'Logged Workouts'"]
        F3["User clicks 'Log Workout' button for final Week 1 workout"]
        F4["That daily workout's details are then displayed and fill the page"]
        F5["As user completes a workout, they input weight and reps for each set of each exercise/lift"]
        F6["At bottom of the workout logs, user then measures energy level, difficulty, and satisfaction levels for that day"]
